# 3. MongoDB schema

We'll start with five collections. Each order belongs to exactly one shop, and all shop-owner queries must be scoped by `shopId`.

## A. User

Shop owners and platform administrators use this collection.

```
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  name: string,
  email: string,
  passwordHash: string,
  role: "shop_owner" | "platform_admin",
  shopIds: ObjectId[],
  isActive: boolean,
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

Use unique normalized email addresses. Passwords must be hashed, never stored as plain text.

## B. Shop

```
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  name: string,
  slug: string,
  ownerIds: ObjectId[],
  status: "active" | "suspended",
  address?: string,
  contactPhone?: string,
  currency: "INR",
  timezone: "Asia/Kolkata",
  settings: {
    maxUploadBytes: number,
    allowedFormats: string[],
    maxCopies: number,
    autoDeleteAfterDays: number
  },
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

Example public URL:

`print.example.com/s/bms-college-prints`

Each shop gets a unique slug and QR code linking directly to its ordering page.

## C. ShopRate

Shop owners configure their own prices.

```
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  shopId: ObjectId,
  paperSize: "A4" | "A3",
  colorMode: "black_white" | "color",
  sides: "single" | "double",
  pricePerSide: number,
  minimumCharge: number,
  effectiveFrom: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

Use one clearly defined pricing unit: price per printed side per sheet, in rupees. This makes single-sided and double-sided calculations easier to explain.

## D. Order

```
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  shopId: ObjectId,
  orderNumber: string,
  customerName?: string,

  status:
    | "processing"
    | "pending"
    | "accepted"
    | "rejected"
    | "completed"
    | "failed",

  files: [{
    originalName: string,
    originalKey: string,
    printPdfKey: string,
    originalMimeType: string,
    pageCount: number
  }],

  printSettings: {
    pageSelection: "all" | "custom",
    pages?: string,
    copies: number,
    colorMode: "black_white" | "color",
    sides: "single" | "double",
    paperSize: "A4" | "A3",
    pagesPerSheet: 1 | 2 | 4
  },

  pricing: {
    estimatedAmount: number,
    currency: "INR",
    rateVersion: string,
    isEstimate: boolean
  },

  rejectionReason?: string,
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date,
  completedAt?: Date
}
```

Use a compound unique index on `{ shopId, orderNumber }`, plus indexes on `{ shopId, status, createdAt }`.

`processing` is important: document conversion can take time, so the shop shouldn't receive a broken or partially processed order.

## E. DailySequence

This collection generates unique, readable queue numbers.

```
{
  _id: string, // shopId + date, e.g. shop123-20261011
  shopId: ObjectId,
  dateKey: string,
  nextNumber: number
}
```

Use an atomic MongoDB increment to allocate numbers. This prevents two students submitting simultaneously from receiving the same number. A shop might see P001, P002, P003, and so on each day.

Important: keep order IDs and internal database IDs separate from public queue numbers. Queue numbers can reset daily; order IDs must not.

## Pricing rules

Calculate the estimated price on the server, not in the browser.

For each document:

1. Count the actual pages in the normalized PDF.
2. Resolve the selected pages and multiply by copies.
3. Calculate physical sheets based on single-sided or double-sided printing and pages per sheet.
4. Apply the shop's matching rate and minimum charge.
5. Store a snapshot of the estimated amount and rate version on the order.

For example, five selected pages, two copies, and a rate of ₹2 per printed side gives an estimated ₹20 for black-and-white single-sided printing, before any minimum charge.

Double-sided printing and multiple pages per sheet need separate calculations. Color pages should use the color rate. These are estimates, not payments or guaranteed final charges.

# 4. API routes

Use `/api/v1` as the prefix. Student routes are public, shop-owner routes require authentication, and platform administration has separate permissions.

| Method  | Endpoint                                             | Purpose                                           |
| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `POST`  | `/auth/register`                                     | Register a shop owner and create their shop       |
| `POST`  | `/auth/login`                                        | Owner login                                       |
| `POST`  | `/auth/logout`                                       | End the session                                   |
| `GET`   | `/auth/me`                                           | Get current user and permitted shops              |
| `GET`   | `/shops/:slug`                                       | Get public shop details and enabled rates         |
| `POST`  | `/shops/:slug/estimate`                              | Calculate a price estimate                        |
| `POST`  | `/shops/:slug/orders`                                | Upload and create an order                        |
| `GET`   | `/orders/:orderId/status`                            | Look up order status using a private lookup token |
| `GET`   | `/owner/shops`                                       | List shops the owner can access                   |
| `GET`   | `/owner/shops/:shopId/orders`                        | Get a shop's paginated order queue                |
| `GET`   | `/owner/shops/:shopId/orders/:orderId`               | View order details                                |
| `GET`   | `/owner/shops/:shopId/orders/:orderId/files/:fileId` | Securely download a print PDF                     |
| `PATCH` | `/owner/shops/:shopId/orders/:orderId/status`        | Accept, reject or complete an order               |
| `GET`   | `/owner/shops/:shopId/rates`                         | View printing rates                               |
| `PUT`   | `/owner/shops/:shopId/rates`                         | Update printing rates                             |
| `PATCH` | `/owner/shops/:shopId/settings`                      | Update shop settings                              |
| `GET`   | `/admin/shops`                                       | Platform-wide shop management                     |
| `PATCH` | `/admin/shops/:shopId/status`                        | Suspend or reactivate a shop                      |

For order creation, use multipart form data containing the file(s) and print settings. The backend validates, converts, counts pages, calculates the estimate, stores the files, and only then publishes the order as pending.

For status changes, enforce valid transitions:

- `processing → pending` after successful document preparation.
- `pending → accepted` or `pending → rejected`.
- `accepted → completed` after the shop finishes the job.
- `processing → failed` if conversion or validation fails.

Rejected orders cannot be completed, and completed orders cannot be reopened through the ordinary status endpoint.

## Real-time updates

Use Socket.IO rooms scoped to the shop:

- `shop:<shopId>:owners` — authorized owners receive new orders and status updates.
- Public order status updates — use an opaque, unguessable lookup token, not a public room that reveals all shop orders.

The dashboard should initially fetch orders via REST, then listen for events. If a WebSocket disconnects, it should reconnect and refetch the queue.

